From ec4a21c3790c5fd517ebdffc5ed5c8c6fa5b8844 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qpzm1258 <qpzm1258@163.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:58:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smsm: Skip mailbox lookup for empty phandles

The SMSM device tree node describes the mailbox of every remote host in
the "mboxes" property. Hosts that have no mailbox are represented by an
empty phandle, e.g. on MSM8916:

	mboxes = <0>, <&apcs 13>, <0>, <&apcs 19>;

smsm_parse_mbox() requests a channel for each host index, which makes
mbox_request_channel() parse the entry at that index. The OF core
reports an empty phandle as -ENOENT, but the mailbox core logs any
parse failure with dev_err(), so the description above produces a
spurious error for every host without a mailbox:

	smsm: mbox_request_channel: can't parse "mboxes" property

A missing mailbox is an expected condition rather than a failure: probe
falls back to the legacy qcom,ipc-N interface for such hosts. Look the
entry up first and only request a channel when the phandle is actually
present, so that the parse error is no longer logged.

Fixes: 75287992f58a ("soc: qcom: smsm: Support using mailbox interface")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: qpzm1258 <qpzm1258@163.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smsm.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smsm.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smsm.c
index 021e9d1f61dc..01125e53f6ea 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smsm.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smsm.c
@@ -376,7 +376,24 @@ static const struct irq_domain_ops smsm_irq_ops = {
 static int smsm_parse_mbox(struct qcom_smsm *smsm, unsigned int host_id)
 {
 	struct smsm_host *host = &smsm->hosts[host_id];
-	int ret = 0;
+	struct of_phandle_args args;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The mboxes property may contain empty phandles (e.g. <0>) to
+	 * indicate that the host at that index simply has no mailbox. The
+	 * OF core reports such an entry as -ENOENT, which
+	 * mbox_request_channel() would otherwise log as a parse failure,
+	 * even though it is an expected condition. Check the entry ourselves
+	 * first so that only real mailboxes are requested; the caller falls
+	 * back to the qcom,ipc-N interface when we return an error.
+	 */
+	ret = of_parse_phandle_with_args(smsm->dev->of_node, "mboxes",
+					 "#mbox-cells", host_id, &args);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	of_node_put(args.np);
 
 	host->mbox_chan = mbox_request_channel(&smsm->mbox_client, host_id);
 	if (IS_ERR(host->mbox_chan)) {
-- 
